{
  "id": "r07",
  "text": "The consequences show up in very ordinary places. On this GameFAQs thread, a player describes upgrading to a larger hard drive and losing their installed demo. It's a personal account, not proof that every hardware change had the same outcome. But look at the subject of the discussion: their console keeps attempting a download that fails. This is the afterlife of the teaser in a help forum, long after the launch mystery. A storage upgrade has become a conversation about something that won't come back. That reverses the original experience rather neatly. Inside the corridor, you wanted a way out. Outside it, you might want a way in. A recording can preserve the rooms, the sound, and the ending, but somebody else is deciding where the camera looks. The software preserves the possibility of making that decision yourself. It can also preserve things nobody thought to point the camera at. Years after the cancellation, Lance McDonald demonstrated why that difference matters.",
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
